2 kΩ resistor is ________ mA.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4a9f814fd307ddb8328eeed4b9255872e08c0a39.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"12"},"solution":"<p>\n 8 (4 - 12)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f727fb9d4cc8b14e8e0bc61227dfa32c9f6d982e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n In the cascode amplifier shown in the figure, if the common-emitter stage (<em>Q</em><sub>1</sub>) has a transconductance <em>g</em><sub><em>m</em>1</sub>, and common base stage (<em>Q</em><sub>2</sub>) has a transductance <em>g</em><sub><em>m</em>2</sub>, then the overall transconductance <img src=\"/media/0c60bd8bd326f4e379ea309ee85e4fb658a2dd5e.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> of the cascode amplifier is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/df18b91ada97fdd805541b81ba81e28b5fdbfea0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7aed18e1f5f1325f37d75079fb5973cf412d8452.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/860572c41a49346a0bd250b83af02f40aadc83ae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7c57f604590339ce66340dccdb93eead2c2ac475.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1d1293ffbcd6dec6d75f1b28ac5b2faefceeeace.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/6e3838a8ef1e3ebfa67a24982e0ec8b9842aefda.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Assuming that the diodes in the below circuit are ideal, the value of labelled voltage ‘<em>V</em>’ is _________ V. (Rounded upto two decimal places)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/22d97013b2931e8381f11475ea94b2963d5414de.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-2.32","high":"-1.23"},"solution":"<p>\n -1.67 (-2.32 - -1.23)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f70a77cec7452e14b3fa93105c9b1f747f79b650.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n In the figure shown below, op-amps have saturation voltage of ±12 V, a capacitor <em>C</em> = 0.02 μF and resistor <em>R</em><sub>1</sub> = 15 kΩ and <em>R</em><sub>2</sub> = 20 kΩ. The value of <em>R</em> to generate 1.2 kHz signal at <em>V</em><sub>01</sub> is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5c4c7a49372566b7aa24ea635f6758fe281cacf0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> = 62 kΩ</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> = 13.88 kΩ</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> = 50 kΩ</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> = 18.65 kΩ</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/255977cdc3b3b71a18c05319e5353d884879467b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The output voltage of circuit shown in figure is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/aa39c28c76653e214a5ae939006640e160e1f308.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n 50 + 20 sin ω<em>t</em> mV</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n 20 + 50 cos ω<em>t</em> mV</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n 20 + 50 sin ω<em>t</em> mV</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n 50 – 20 cos ω<em>t</em> mV</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/91f8e14db8f8e66c7ea5ce2737b2c04f1406d27e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n For the given network with Vin as 5.2 V, desired output level is 0 V. Assuming <em>V<sub>BE</sub></em> as 0.712 V and <em>R</em><sub>1</sub> as 1.47 kΩ, the constant current <img src=\"/media/39b7ec2958ac1f7566f0ae0c978bac5ae16a0b4b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> supplied by transistor <em>Q</em><sub>1</sub> is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d95cf68c0bf2b0afdd05194aebf3226b5f3392d1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2.923 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 2.568 mA</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 2.84 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 2.125 mA</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/36a27d5ad9864c45761a56498621eb99d1ffe6b2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A non-inverting amplifier shown in figure has the input voltage <em>V<sub>s</sub></em> = 100 mV with a source resistance of <em>R<sub>s</sub></em> = 500 Ω. The circuit parameters are <em>R<sub>F</sub></em> = 398 kΩ, <em>R</em><sub>1</sub> = 5 kΩ and A<sub>0</sub> = 2 × 10<sup>5</sup>. The percentage error in the output voltage <em>V</em><sub>0</sub> and the gain <em>A<sub>f</sub></em> compared to when A0 tends to infinity is given by</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a49ee74f1c0aba13d6b0853bea760a285c4e0cbe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/bd0427268d6b3290b84eb4f8fa87bc149b5812d3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7f3039eba8a830504213ed8f8d9415052838c9c9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/f61c5d0a7c43d63d28877b1249fdeed6281bf7c4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c8f8252d226418afd3f3b4dddaf3edf3a07ed46c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5bdc7b771fa242041f0775a30a7f531cbef2fb1c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n For an op-amp shown in figure, the input offset voltage is 12 mV, the biasing current is 500 mA and input offset current is 90 nA. Consider <img src=\"/media/559bf7cef5a3f02ee79c84e799f1ab243240fbcd.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3271379cab10053f81c21ba62d7d7492926a3bf3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Total output offset voltage with compensating resistor is given by</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 132 mV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 162 mV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 118 mV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 141 mV</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/081b2741f7a607a532fc9feb35eaa91413a1682e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p>\n  </p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/749bff274af178bab8596614d44c7633ef4e4de9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The transistor is biased in such a way that it is operating with <em>g<sub>m</sub></em> = 40 mA/V and β = 100. The value of corner frequency due to capacitor <em>C</em><sub>1</sub> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 10.59 Hz</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 105.9 Hz</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1.059 Hz</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 159.05 Hz</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b4987190dff8f0a7cb40153a5e33f5d9edb4b837.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n The closed loop gain <img src=\"/media/8963c70489b2d5bfcc2eba5aa6ad50a1cc3fb338.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> of the feedback circuit shown in figure below is: (Assume early voltage as infinity)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/55ff4ffb6585eb17a2d5b3efeded40354645f8d5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/49e333c8e1f113dac66e112344e2ec4585a2d950.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2195d462aae675f08f81aae95660d7ed17ade2a2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7127865254060681a35e400ced8aaf241751e42b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/bd9e328b28227f7375c1f8554e0b013b509133ff.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1a8fbfbf72778659aac1d44a7e17ddef49524e67.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n For the network shown in figure, the range of <img src=\"/media/81ad81470f670583dd40e5bbe33ed729beaa1527.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> that will maintain <em>V<sub>L</sub></em> at 8 V and not exceed the maximum power rating of the zener diode is given by</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/98b4be7b3fa34125316dda3e442a748ed6006315.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 7.86 V to 11.3 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> –15.86 V to 7.86 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> –11.3 V to 15.86 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 11.3 V to 15.86 V</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/e45aaf4447fcb6b6bf48cac0a5f4a48f9f3aa5e2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c6d650bc3b7de9c5cf99d065cf18e1cd39f504cf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n For the Schmitt trigger shown in the figure, <em>V</em><sub>sat</sub> = ±13.5 V. If the resistances have tolerance of ±5%, the minimum hysteresis is _________.</p>\n<p>\n (Rounded upto 2 decimal places)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/75e43101a15c099aa5cd139ff4d8da595e57abbe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.48","high":"0.61"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.53 (0.48 - 0.61)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d7c7490002483458be7d349153bc1aa5807f258e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/bbbb0bf40616a1b2f7a8b95d48032cf48618bd52.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The value of I for the network shown below is:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9358e010b068b63cab4de573cb26c2ed001c7721.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 18.45 mA</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.851 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1.845 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 19.3 mA</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ce3b3921b5bf7b27e78f5f72d2b35e6766f347de.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following circuit,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f441a9b2bb1e642543cf10746fc7630a601b138c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n If <img src=\"/media/9abafaf7ccf5332f6138b502e010702303a89dde.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and <img src=\"/media/82579934c2a2c82dc0736f5538851043dca1a57d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = Early voltage = 120 V both for n and p devices. The small signal voltage gain of the amplifier circuit is _________. (Rounded to nearest integer value)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-130","high":"-110"},"solution":"<p>\n -120 (-130 - -110)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/dba6ee663f16a05500c22b94769ddc2b438467fc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/2946721ea899fff7944b8164e36190aec481dfe6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n The open-circuit (<em>R<sub>L</sub></em> = ∞) voltage gain of the ac equivalent source follower circuit shown in figure is AV = 0.98. When <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> is set to 1 kΩ, the voltage gain is reduced to <em>A<sub>V</sub></em> = 0.49. The values of <em>g<sub>m</sub></em> and <em>r</em><sub>0</sub> are given by</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/e6d30786d128a39c349ff3031c8703a9cf81098d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/76a1ac5f1dbf6acf37579b691e934f65695b021f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/34df06849e0d3993138072e643a748fb710c20c6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ecca8d3b6a34bf138477372f0a36efde7e18c130.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/40216e1276d0606fe8363c774ad711a9cab5a0f5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/19c6ff24bce77206318fdf8918624e603b570a40.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/823c6542f5db70fb632d2568ad8bd8982aab446c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n The input voltage to the half wave rectifier with capacitor filter is <img src=\"/media/f7d2d2a9b967d1a3de59ab531b553254d96fa3ba.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" />Assume a diode cut-in voltage of<img src=\"/media/599bd33249548320d132f4bf035988f48c6dfa19.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The peak to peak ripple voltage is to be no more than <em>V<sub>r</sub></em>  = 4 V. If the filter capacitor is 50 μF, the minimum load resistance that can be connected to the output is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2.256 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 6.08 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 31.25 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 22.56 kΩ</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/7f849cd0f5ad73f59380edec085591ce7bdbc71c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c574f19a507d8897666d1d0434a06b151150246a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n For the circuit shown in figure the transistor parameters are : <em>K</em><sub><em>n</em>1</sub> = 0.2 mA/V<sup>2</sup>,<em>K</em><sub><em>n</em>2</sub> = <em>K</em><sub><em>n</em>3</sub> = <em>K</em><sub><em>n</em>4</sub> = 0.1 mA/V<sup>2</sup>, and <em>V</em><sub><em>TN</em>1</sub> = <em>V</em><sub><em>TN</em>2</sub> = <em>V</em><sub><em>TN</em>3</sub> = <em>V</em><sub><em>TN</em>4</sub> = 1 V.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3d2e7b42d128b542c6e743d3a2736ac7312bc547.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The value of <img src=\"/media/28cef030fae75c99ddceb4402ad38b53ffe13d6c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> (in mA) is _________. [Rounded upto 2 decimal places]</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.19","high":"0.26"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.22 (0.19 - 0.26)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/57fdbdc48f4666059046e5b0fe650cf54e349529.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/78551fb8674c6d06461f6810992f7e6af6b6ed8e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the circuit given below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5f91de8d2aad9279a25c711d21b3d542ba299072.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Assume the diode is ideal. The average current passing through the resistor <em>R</em> is found to be 5 mA. Then the value of resistance <em>R</em> is equal to ________ kΩ.</p>\n<p>\n (Round upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.42","high":"0.49"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.47 (0.42 - 0.49)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/206a537f99b1ca3277e387afa82f39517e6693ae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d266be97bacb2f27731828253a28241fb0c48726.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/846be885029782845a24814c79cd58c88c3757d0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n A diode <em>D</em><sub>1</sub> is connected in parallel with a diode <em>D</em><sub>2</sub> with reverse saturation current equal to 10<sup>–11</sup> A and 10<sup>–9</sup> A respectively. The diodes are connected across a voltage source (<em>V<sub>s</sub></em>) in series with a resistance of 3 kΩ. Then the value of voltage <em>V<sub>s</sub></em> in (V) is approximately equal to _________. (Assume η = 2 and <em>V<sub>T</sub></em> = 26 mV) (Rounded upto 1 decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12.4","high":"13.2"},"solution":"<p>\n 12.8 (12.4 - 13.2)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0a1910d782f1a0e4bbfc6496acf8b6ab316c91c4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n For given circuit, the load current <img src=\"/media/c08de4d28db7d84e844dd7c5aa78b5c33f215f1c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is __________ mA. (Rounded upto two decimal places)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/75c049e46903e6a3153a552e10a2644f96ca0344.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"5.25","high":"6.35"},"solution":"<p>\n 5.71 (5.25 - 6.35)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/405db67402bc8aff767b5566c8c1258d1b983dd2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":22,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Both the transistors have β<sub>0</sub> = 150 and operated at <img src=\"/media/4fcdcffead3738a5dacb6ecc1a3ad8d9342a1352.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 2.5 mA. Assume <em>R<sub>s</sub></em> = 0.85 kΩ and <em>R<sub>C</sub></em> = 1.8 kΩ. <em>V</em><sub>T</sub> = 26 mV, <em>r</em><sub>0</sub> = ∞.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a41197f33819dadb52c62ce889f20e336820d9e9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The overall voltage gain <em>A<sub>V</sub></em> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> –9002.509</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1312.786</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 9002.509</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> –1312.786</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8dff40ad7d04602bb684ea8992cfab65315dcdc6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/e3252b7be1594d2cbaf550c457cfa8471fb31521.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":23,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the shunt-shunt feedback amplifier shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d16c0da016d43f4bc8cde02a90758cfc19c26be9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n If the transistor is biased at <img src=\"/media/fa40f2510f62bd1258ca9915d25482a2fea2c35f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 4.32 mA, then the value of output resistance <em>R</em><sub>0</sub> is equal to _______ Ω. [<em>V<sub>T</sub></em> = 26 mV] (Rounded upto one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"79.5","high":"86.7"},"solution":"<p>\n 82.9 (79.5 - 86.7)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b3650ed9186de3c3bd68b402ad29027dba0047a5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/10984cecbad3dd10f09a5988f7ebf9bdcd53658a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the amplifier circuit shown in figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8cfd98bf3113fd5eea32e6f932a21673da7cc0bd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The transistors parameters are <em>V</em><sub><em>EB</em>(ON)</sub> = 0.7 V, β = 80, <em>V<sub>T</sub></em> = 26 mV and <em>V<sub>A</sub></em> = ∞. Then the value of small signal voltage gain is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> –26.24 V/V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1.931 V/V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 26.24 V/V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> –1.931 V/V</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/15259bce025246831deaaa71a31a930347c71248.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/81b8f12f41b7cf592d64c2a6b4a94eb9726b4077.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n For a modified current mirror shown in figure, the current through collector resistor <em>R<sub>C</sub></em> is ________ mA. Assume <em>V<sub>BE</sub></em> = 0.7 V and β = 100.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/39daf0c0d5610abdae8194362c1d9f9a9ae75f70.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3.256","high":"4.825"},"solution":"<p>\n 4.125 (3.256 - 4.825)</p>\n<p>\n <img src